    "guidance": "Experimental/specialized, not a default: h04 passed only 5/12 validations from its own demonstrated entry states. Use, if at all, with strict external monitoring when object_pose and target_pose are reliable, the drawer is open/stable, the block is plausibly held close to the TCP, and a coherent close-to-separated transition is expected. Its proximity-gated object-to-destination frame is intended to combine attached transport with fixture-anchored retreat, but no out-of-distribution benefit was observed. In the five passes, first exit attainment was at steps 172–221 and final drawer_position was 0.277–0.300. Four of the seven failed runs transiently met the exit but then closed the drawer with the block inside; those runs had full-task success but violated this skill’s required open-drawer exit. The other three ended with the object outside and drawer_position <=0.083. Thus do not treat a transient in-cavity event as durable: stop or hand off promptly once two frames confirm an inside, floor-height, stationary, detached block while drawer_position remains >0.26. Avoid noisy/chattering object–TCP distance, uncertain attachment, premature drops, or unreachable targets. Watch for reference-weight collapse while the block should be held, weight persistence/chatter after release, opening outside the cavity, a block above floor height or following retreat, drawer closure before handoff, and IK/limit warnings. Switch to h02 once separated/deposited, h03 for near-nominal release ambiguity, and invoke close_drawer only after observed stationarity and separation."
